## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-cloud IaC security policy gates using industry-standard tools (tfsec, Checkov); covers secret management, encryption, versioning, provider pinning, tagging, and backend security.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets in code and tfvars detection
- Cloud storage encryption and versioning
- Provider version pinning and backends
- Tagging and access controls across clouds
- CI integration and local verification for IaC gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Failing: plaintext secret in Terraform
variable \"db_password\" { default = \"SuperSecret123\" }
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = var.db_password
}

// Passing: secret retrieved from Secrets Manager
data \"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\" \"db_pass\" {
  secret_id = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:region:acct:secret:db-password\"
}
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db_pass.secret_string
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit-test this gate locally? 
- How would you evolve checks for multi-cloud secret fetch patterns?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to craft a concrete, beginner-friendly CI gate that enforces per-container resource budgeting and a basic security posture—practical patterns seen in production.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes manifest traversal
- GitHub Actions CI gates
- resources.requests/limits
- securityContext basics (readOnlyRootFilesystem, allowPrivilegeEscalation)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js pseudo-check using js-yaml
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const path = './manifests';
for (const f of fs.readdirSync(path)) {
  if (!f.endsWith('.yaml')) continue;
  const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path + '/' + f, 'utf8'));
  const containers = (doc?.spec?.template?.spec?.containers) || [];
  for (const c of containers) {
    if (!c.resources?.requests || !c.resources?.limits) fail();
    if (c.securityContext?.readOnlyRootFilesystem !== true) fail();
    if (c.securityContext?.allowPrivilegeEscalation !== false) fail();
  }
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle multi-namespace repos?
- How would you surface results in PR checks?
